y insight is that the system of SDEs can be reduced to a 3D Itô SDE with time-dependent diffusion. The velocity variance squared for each component evolves as:\n$$\\frac{d(\\langle p_i^2/2 \\rangle)}{dt} = \\frac{d}{dt} \\left( -\\frac{1}{2} \\langle \\dot{p}_i^2 \\rangle \\right) = -\\frac{1}{2} \\langle 2 \\dot{p}_i \\ddot{p}_i + \\dot{p}_i^2 \\rangle$$\n\nFrom the SDE, $\\dot{p}_i = -\\mu p_i + \\sqrt{\\kappa} dW_i$, so $\\ddot{p}_i = -\\dot{\\mu} p_i - \\mu \\dot{p}_i + \\sqrt{\\kappa} dW_i = (-\\dot{\\mu} - \\mu^2) p_i + \\sqrt{\\kappa} dW_i$.\n\nThus,\n$$\\langle \\dot{p}_i \\ddot{p}_i \\rangle = (-\\dot{\\mu} - \\mu^2) \\langle p_i^2 \\rangle - \\mu \\langle p_i^2 \\rangle + \\text{Correction from } dW$$\n\nSince $\\langle p_i^2 \\rangle = \\langle (\\dot{p}_i)^2 \\rangle \\cdot \\langle(-\\dot{\\mu} - \\mu^2) p_i^2 \\rangle + \\text{finite terms}$, and for the variance:\n$$\\frac{d(\\text{Var}(p_i))}{dt} = 2 \\langle \\dot{p}_i \\ddot{p}_i \\rangle - 2 \\langle \\dot{p}_i^2 \\rangle = 2 \\langle (-\\dot{\\mu} - \\mu^2) p_i^2 - \\mu p_i^2 \\rangle d\\mu - 2 \\langle \\kappa \\cdot dW \\rangle$$\n\nIntegrating gives:\n$$\\text{Var}(p_i(\\tau)) - \\text{Var}(p_i(\\tau_0)) = \\int_0^\\tau 2 (2 \\mu \\text{Var}(p_i(\\tau\')) - (\\dot{\\mu} + \\mu^2) \\text{Var}(p_i(\\tau\')) \\cdot d\\mu(\\tau\')) f(\\tau) d\\tau$$\n\nFor our case, $\\mu(\\tau) = a T^2(\\tau) = a T_0^2 (\\tau_0/\\tau)^2$, so $\\dot{\\mu}(\\tau) = 2 a T_0^2 \\tau_0 (\\tau_0/\\tau)^{5/3}$.\n\nWith the initial variance term $\\langle p_x^2(\\tau_0)/2 \\rangle - \\langle p_x(\\tau_0)^2/2 \\rangle = p_0^2/2$, and if we assume that the systematic term $2 \\mu \\text{Var}(p) - (\\dot{\\mu} + \\mu^2) \\text{Var}(p) \\approx -2 \\mu \\text{Var}(p)$ (since $\\dot{\\mu}/\\mu \\approx d\\mu(\\tau)/d\\tau = -2 a T_0^2 \\tau_0 / \\tau^{5/3}$, which is large negative), we might get an approximation. But the problem asks for an exact solution.\n\nActually, for finite-dimensional maps, these processes are convert